# ── Cycle-demo version ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Run with:  npm run dev:cycle     (or  npm run build:cycle  for a build)
# Every scan shows the NEXT result in the loop — Male → Female → Female
# Pregnant → back to Male — regardless of what the camera sees (even empty
# photos advance the cycle). No server or API needed. The loop lives in
# src/lib/api.ts (cycleStates); edit there to change the cycle.
#
# NOTE: the PRODUCTION build (`npm run build`, what Render runs on deploy)
# now uses this file too — so the deployed version cycles as well. To deploy
# the real (API-backed) version again, set VITE_CYCLE_MODE=false as an env
# var in your host's dashboard (it overrides this file), or revert the
# "build" script in package.json to plain `vite build`.
VITE_CYCLE_MODE=true
